### Central Thesis
PlaqueBoyMax is a textbook Type 3: he fused identity with achievement when he named himself after a trophy at 17, and his entire career, from the relentless streaming to the hollow milestones to the Streamer University shame collapse, is one long project of closing the gap between the name and the proof.

### Thread Map
Every section serves that thesis, and the chain holds: cold open (name taken from a trophy) → diagnosis (the pattern named: runs on evidence, not stimulation) → childhood (where results-for-freedom was learned) → live engineer (the machine that mints proof for other people) → trophy ledger (the audit: his name is on the frame, never the voice) → can't log off (why wins don't hold: the counter resets at midnight) → Streamer University (what happens when the image itself is attacked and there's no persona to absorb it) → Madison Square Garden (the one trophy that would close the gap). The ledger table, the hollow million-follower moment, and the lunch-table empathy turn form the spine, and all three were left untouched.

